/*
 * lsp — the diagnostics of a compilation, as a language server publishes them.
 *
 * An ErrorMsg tree is flattened into the failures it holds, as `reports` does
 * for the terminal, but each of them becomes an LSP `Diagnostic` instead of a
 * rendered report: a range, a severity, a code and a message, the places its
 * notes and context frames name as related information, and the edits it
 * proposes as quick fixes. Nothing is read back from the rendered text.
 * `Flattening` builds them, `JsonExporting` writes them as the objects the
 * protocol carries.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::errors::lsp
 * @File: ymirc/errors/lsp.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-26
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
